<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#chiefdom">Glossary</a> · Term · government</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chiefdom</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 5000 BCE – present</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The chiefdom was the form in which many farming and fishing peoples first lived under permanent rulers: a hereditary chief at the head of ranked kin, fed by tribute and upheld by ritual rather than by officials.</p></div>
